-- title:
--   Semistable model with descent from a disc-charted covering, q=3
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q = 3$, $M'$ is a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $\ell$ is a prime with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. (In the later binders the letter `ℓ` is reused for an index running over [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) $= \mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{F}_q)$, shadowing this prime; such indices are written $\lambda$ below.) Further, $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$, and $W$ is a finite set of places of the level-$M'$ modular function field `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ (the subfield of Laurent series generated by the reductions of the two $j$-series), characterised by `hW` as consisting exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`. The hypothesis `hle` records the inclusion of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field, into $F :=$ `fieldBar q M'`, the function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the curve of level structure `levelH q M'` inside level $q^2M'$.
--
--   The reduction datum consists of a `ConstantReduction` $R_0$ of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` — a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ together with a surjective residue homomorphism onto the characteristic-$p$ modular function field whose kernel is the maximal ideal, contracting to $A$ on constants, extending the reduction $A \to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, with a scaling clause, and a degree-preserving map on places compatible with pushforward of divisors — and of the compatibility `hR₀`: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. An element $\pi \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is given with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ and $\pi \in A$, together with a ring homomorphism from the field `GaloisField q 2` to $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, the assumption that the Drinfeld coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, and an index $\zeta$ of a primitive $q$-th root of unity.
--
--   Two families of valuation subrings of $F$ are given: Igusa rings $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_\lambda$ for $\lambda \in \mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{F}_q)$ and supersingular rings $O^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$ for $s \in W$. The Igusa clauses are: `hIg_inf`, saying that $f$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ at the line at infinity precisely when $f$, as a Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, is a quotient of two Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ the denominator of which has non-zero coefficientwise reduction; `hIg`, saying that for every line $\lambda$ there is $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with `redQ q γ • lineInfty q = λ` and $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_\lambda$ the contraction of $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_{\infty}$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj`, the injectivity of $\lambda \mapsto O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_\lambda$; and `hIg_perm`, saying that for every root-of-unity index $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ the contractions along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permute the family. The supersingular clauses are: `hSS_A`, that $O^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$ contracts to $A$ on constants; `hSS_over`, that for $s \in W$ and $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ having non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` at which the $q$-expansion of $j$ has non-negative order, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation ring of $s$, the image of $f$ in $F$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$ and, for every $a \in A$ whose reduction equals the value of the $R_0$-residue of $f$ at $s$, the difference of that image and $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$; `hSS_fix`, that each $O^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$ is fixed by contraction along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr`, that each $O^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$ contains an element $t$ with $t - a$ a unit of $O^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$ for every $a \in A$.
--
--   A `SemistableCovering` $\mathcal{C}$ of $F$ over $A$ indexed by $W$ is given: component charts $C^{\mathrm{Ig}}_\lambda$ on fields $F^{\mathrm{Ig}}_\lambda$ and $C^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$ on fields $F^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$, annuli $\mathcal{A}_{\lambda,s}$ and $\mathcal{A}'_{\lambda,s}$ with nodes $x^{\mathrm{s}}_{\lambda,s}$, $x^{\mathrm{t}}_{\lambda,s}$, together with its structural clauses (matching domains and moduli, non-zero modulus, the product relation between the two parameters, attachment of the annuli to the charts at the nodes, the unique matching of nodes with indices, and the partition of the places of $F$). The hypothesis `h9` is a ten-fold conjunction: the chart integer rings are the prescribed ones, $(C^{\mathrm{Ig}}_\lambda).\mathrm{integers} = O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_\lambda$ and $(C^{\mathrm{ss}}_s).\mathrm{integers} = O^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$; and $\mathcal{C}$ satisfies `EquivClauses` (for each root-of-unity index and each $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ a permutation of $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{F}_q)$ matching the contracted charts' integer rings and domains, the supersingular charts being preserved, and matching annulus domains and moduli), `LevelPinClauses hle R₀` (the supersingular charts read $R_0$-residues through evaluation at $s$, and each Igusa chart carries a ring homomorphism from the characteristic-$p$ modular function field compatible with residues and with membership in the valuation ring of $x^{\mathrm{s}}_{\lambda,s}$), `InertiaClause π` (for inertia elements of tame character $1$ at $\pi$, the arithmetic Galois action preserves all charts, their place maps and domains, and fixes the annulus parameters), `WidthClause ⟨π, hπP⟩` (each annulus modulus is a unit of $A$ times a positive power of $\pi$), `GenusClause` (the genus identity relating the genus of $F$ and the numbers of components to the genera of the $F^{\mathrm{Ig}}_\lambda$ and $F^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$ and the number of nodes), `DiscFibreClause` (all charts have disc fibres), `CurveClause` (each $F^{\mathrm{Ig}}_\lambda$ and $F^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$ is a curve over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, essentially of finite type), and `NaturalityClauses` (equivariance of the supersingular charts under inertia and under the level automorphisms for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, invariance of the chart at the line at infinity under unipotent level automorphisms, and a root-of-unity index $\zeta_0$ for which the Igusa family is permuted according to `redQ`).
--
--   The chart hypotheses `hIgCharts` and `hSSCharts` require every chart to be disc-charted: for each line $\lambda$, respectively each $s \in W$, there are a `RegularProlongation` $R$ of $A$ with the same integer ring as the chart and the same residue map on it, a family of sets of places $\mathrm{disc}(Q)$ and coordinates $\mathrm{coord}(Q)$ forming an `R.DiscFamily` for the chart's node set (each non-node $Q$ has $\mathrm{disc}(Q)$ a residue disc with coordinate $\mathrm{coord}(Q)$, and distinct non-nodes have disjoint discs), the chart's domain is the union of the $\mathrm{disc}(Q)$ over non-nodes $Q$, and the chart's place map is constantly $Q$ on $\mathrm{disc}(Q)$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hNoPkgSS` is a cusp-free-package exclusion at the nodes of the supersingular charts: for every $s \in W$, every regular prolongation $R$ agreeing with $C^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$ in integer ring and residue map, every node $Q$ of $C^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$, every subring $S$ of $F$, every ring homomorphism $\varphi_T$ from $A[X]$ to $S$, every ring homomorphism $\chi_0 : S \to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ and every set $D$ of places of $F$, the conjunction of the following clauses (summarised here) fails: $S$ contains the constants from $A$; $\varphi_T$ is formally smooth and formally unramified and restricts to the constants on $A$, with $\chi_0 \circ \varphi_T$ the reduction on constants and $\chi_0(\varphi_T X) = 0$; for every $c \in A$ of zero reduction there is a unique $A$-point of $S$ fixing the constants, reducing to $\chi_0$ and sending $\varphi_T X$ to $c$; $S$ is read by $R$ into the valuation ring of $Q$ with residues given by $\chi_0$; the $R$-residue of $\varphi_T X$ has order $1$ at $Q$; $D$ consists exactly of the rational places at which all elements of $S$ are integral with values in $A$, the values of $f \in S$ being non-units precisely when $\chi_0(f) = 0$; every $A$-point of $S$ compatible with the constants and with $\chi_0$ arises from a unique place of $D$; at each place of $D$ the valuation ring consists of the quotients of elements of $S$; functions of order zero at every place of $D$ become units of $S$ after scaling by a non-zero constant; every element of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ integral at all places of $D$ lies in $S$; and the image in $F$ of the $q$-expansion of $j$ has non-negative order at every place of $D$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hJ'` pins $j$ at each supersingular place: for each $s \in W$ there is $a \in A$ such that the difference of the $q$-expansion of $j$ and $a$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, has non-negative order at every place where $j$ does, its $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation ring of $s$, and that residue has value $0$ at $s$. The hypothesis `hIgJ` says that whenever such a pinned difference has $R_0$-residue in the valuation ring of $s$ with value $0$ there, then for every line $\lambda$ and every place $Q$ of $F^{\mathrm{Ig}}_\lambda$ at which the $C^{\mathrm{Ig}}_\lambda$-residue of the image of that difference is integral with residue $0$, the place $Q$ is a node of $C^{\mathrm{Ig}}_\lambda$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hAnRing` supplies, for each $s \in W$, a regular prolongation $R$ agreeing with $C^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$ in integer ring and residue map, together with crossing data: an index type $\Lambda$ of layers with subrings $C'_l \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ contained in $A$, each a discrete valuation domain with uniformiser $\varpi'_l$, a base layer $l_0$, complete discrete valuation domains $W_l$ with elements $\pi_l$, exponents $E_l$ and $E_0$, subrings $\mathcal{N}_\lambda$ and local noetherian subrings $\mathcal{N}_{\lambda,l}$ of $F$, and coordinates $x_\lambda, y_\lambda, u_\lambda \in F$, subject to the clauses (summarised here): the maximal ideal of $C'_l$ is generated by $\varpi'_l$ in the sense that vanishing of the reduction of $d \in C'_l$ is divisibility by $\varpi'_l$; $C'_{l_0} \le C'_l$; $\varpi'_{l_0} \ne 0$; $A$ is algebraic over $C'_{l_0}$; each $\pi_l$ is irreducible and $E_l \ge 1$; and, for every line $\lambda$: the parameter of $\mathcal{A}_{\lambda,s}$ is $y_\lambda$ and its modulus is $\varpi'^{\,E_0}_{l_0}$; the nodes $x^{\mathrm{s}}_{\lambda,s}$, $x^{\mathrm{t}}_{\lambda,s}$ and all places of the annulus domain are rational; $\mathcal{N}_\lambda$ consists of the elements integral for $C^{\mathrm{Ig}}_\lambda$, for $R$ and at all places of the annulus, their values at those places lying in $A$; the crossing relation $x_\lambda y_\lambda = \varpi'^{\,E_0}_{l_0} u_\lambda$ holds; $x_\lambda$ reduces to $0$ on the Igusa chart and its $R$-residue has order $1$ at $x^{\mathrm{t}}_{\lambda,s}$, while $y_\lambda$ has $R$-residue $0$ and Igusa residue of order $1$ at $x^{\mathrm{s}}_{\lambda,s}$; every element of $F$ is a quotient of elements of some $\mathcal{N}_{\lambda,l}$, and a constant combination of elements of $\mathcal{N}_{\lambda,l_0}$ over a denominator; and, for each layer $l$, the chain $\mathcal{N}_{\lambda,l_0} \le \mathcal{N}_{\lambda,l} \le \mathcal{N}_\lambda$, the characterisation of the annulus domain as the places at which $\mathcal{N}_{\lambda,l}$ is integral and non-units take values in the maximal ideal of $A$, the inclusion of the constants $C'_l$, a residue-field clause (every $g$ differs from a constant by a non-unit), preservation of $C'_l$-linear independence, a node-chart clause exhibiting $\mathcal{N}_{\lambda,l}$ as the localisation at its non-units of a subring $B_x$ generated over the constants by a finite set and containing $x_\lambda, y_\lambda, u_\lambda$, the memberships $x_\lambda, y_\lambda \in \mathcal{N}_{\lambda,l}$ with $u_\lambda$ a unit there, and finally a ring homomorphism $\sigma$ from $W_l$ to the adic completion of $\mathcal{N}_{\lambda,l}$ and an isomorphism $\iota$ of that completion with the crossing model `UVCrossingModel (Wc l) (π l ^ E l)`, sending $\pi_l$ to the constant $\varpi'_l$, constants to constants, hitting every constant from $C'_l$, and reading the orders at $x^{\mathrm{s}}_{\lambda,s}$ and $x^{\mathrm{t}}_{\lambda,s}$ as the exponents of $V$ modulo $(\pi_l, U)$, respectively of $U$ modulo $(\pi_l, V)$, up to a unit.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion asserts the existence of a semistable model $M$ of type [`AlgebraicCurve.SemistableModel`](def/AlgebraicCurve_SemistableModel.html#L34) over $A$ for the field $F$, with vertex index $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{F}_q) \sqcup W$ carrying the residue fields `𝒞.sumFbar` and the charts `𝒞.sumChart` (the Igusa charts on the left summands, the supersingular charts on the right), with edge index $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{F}_q) \times W$ carrying the annuli $(\lambda,s) \mapsto \mathcal{A}_{\lambda,s}$, source $\lambda$ and target $s$, and with the two node-place families given by `𝒞.sumNode` at the source and the target, that is $(\lambda,s) \mapsto x^{\mathrm{s}}_{\lambda,s}$ and $(\lambda,s) \mapsto x^{\mathrm{t}}_{\lambda,s}$; such that the type `M.Descent` is non-empty. Thus $M$ is an integral scheme $X$, proper, flat and locally of finite presentation over $\operatorname{Spec} A$, with an isomorphism of $F$ with the function field of $X$ compatible with the constants from $A$, and with points of $X$ attached to the places of $F$, to the charts, to the non-node places of each chart's residue field and to the edges, subject to the defining clauses of `SemistableModel` (prescribed local rings, the classification bijection identifying $X$ with the disjoint union of the generic point, these point families, and the specialisation and crossing clauses), summarised here. Non-emptiness of `M.Descent` asserts in addition the existence of descent data: a noetherian henselian local ring $A_0$ with an injective local homomorphism $A_0 \to A$, a subfield $K_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose intersection with $A$ is the image of $A_0$ and over which $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is algebraic, surjectivity of $A_0 \to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, an integral scheme $X_0$ proper, flat and locally of finite presentation over $\operatorname{Spec} A_0$, an isomorphism of $X$ with the pullback of $X_0$ along $\operatorname{Spec} A \to \operatorname{Spec} A_0$ compatible with the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and with generic points, and a subfield $F_0 \subseteq F$ with $F$ algebraic over $F_0$ and an isomorphism of $F_0$ with the function field of $X_0$ compatible with the identification of $F$ with the function field of $X$. No uniqueness of $M$ is asserted.
--
--   This is the global assembly step at $q = 3$ and rigid auxiliary level: a semistable covering of the full-level modular function field by Igusa and supersingular charts, all of whose charts are residue-disc charted and whose nodes carry crossing models over layered discrete valuation rings, is converted into an actual semistable model over the valuation ring $A$ which descends to a henselian noetherian subring. It is used in the construction of the semistable covering with its equivalence clauses from a given semistable model, the two statements together tying the chart-theoretic and scheme-theoretic descriptions of the reduction of the modular curve at $q$.
